WEBVTT

00:18.018 --> 00:19.978
There's a fire burning
at the back of the building!

00:25.442 --> 00:29.195
Find the one who murdered Momoka,
then burn them in the Fire of Judgment.

00:29.279 --> 00:32.282
A witch hunt? This sounds interesting.

00:33.992 --> 00:35.368
The game has already begun.

00:36.411 --> 00:37.662
Hey.

00:39.956 --> 00:42.250
All right, let's search for the witch!

00:57.432 --> 00:58.475
Hey, you.

01:00.018 --> 01:02.020
Why weren't you with her today?

01:02.103 --> 01:02.937
What?

01:03.521 --> 01:06.441
Why were you late?
Weren't you always with her?

01:07.525 --> 01:09.569
- Is she the witch?
- It's not me!

01:09.652 --> 01:11.279
We'll know once we throw you in the fire!

01:11.362 --> 01:12.989
I was in my room! I'm not lying!

01:13.073 --> 01:16.284
You two were always together,
but today you happened to not be with her?

01:17.827 --> 01:21.331
All right, it's decided. She's the witch!
Drag her to the fire!

01:22.040 --> 01:23.917
- Come on!
- Hoist her up!

01:24.584 --> 01:26.002
- Heave-ho!
- Stop it!

01:26.086 --> 01:27.796
- Here we go!
- I didn't do anything!

01:28.379 --> 01:29.422
Stop this!

01:29.506 --> 01:30.965
Calm down.

01:31.758 --> 01:33.134
Let go of Asahi.

01:34.094 --> 01:35.762
There should be other suspects.

01:38.973 --> 01:42.352
Where were you guys,
and what were you doing? Can you prove it?

01:43.436 --> 01:44.562
Just say it!

01:47.232 --> 01:50.485
Both of us were having
a good time in the same room, right?

01:52.487 --> 01:55.907
Everyone will take turns reporting
what they've been doing in the past hour.

01:57.117 --> 01:58.243
There's blood on her!

02:01.913 --> 02:04.666
- Don't get the wrong idea.
- Now, this is getting interesting.

02:04.749 --> 02:06.751
- Could she be the witch?
- You're wrong!

02:06.835 --> 02:08.378
This is Hatter's blood.

02:09.087 --> 02:10.630
- What?
- Hatter's blood?

02:11.422 --> 02:14.509
I was checking Hatter's body.
That was when the blood got on it.

02:15.218 --> 02:16.302
His body?

02:19.347 --> 02:20.974
Hatter was murdered.

02:22.475 --> 02:25.228
- Hatter was…
- Why did you keep it from us?

02:26.062 --> 02:29.482
The executives believed
this would throw everyone into confusion.

02:30.066 --> 02:33.528
Are you guys hiding
more things from us? Hey!

02:33.611 --> 02:36.239
- Stop whispering among yourselves!
- Calm down!

02:40.118 --> 02:42.370
This bullet was stuck
inside Hatter's body.

02:43.371 --> 02:45.957
The firing marks align
with the firearms we have here.

02:46.583 --> 02:47.625
What?

02:48.418 --> 02:52.672
This means someone
at the Beach killed Hatter.

02:56.593 --> 03:01.222
Hey. Could it be
that the witch killed Hatter?

03:03.433 --> 03:06.477
I mean, doesn't that sound plausible
given the timing of the events?

03:06.561 --> 03:08.646
The witch must be among them--

03:14.152 --> 03:15.320
How troublesome.

03:16.070 --> 03:17.906
Let's just burn everyone we find.

03:22.744 --> 03:24.913
If someone among us is the witch,

03:27.415 --> 03:28.374
then everyone

03:28.458 --> 03:30.210
other than the militant member
is the witch.

03:32.837 --> 03:34.214
Who's the witch?

03:34.839 --> 03:35.840
Come forward.

03:42.430 --> 03:43.806
If nobody does,

03:44.933 --> 03:46.768
then I'll throw everyone into the fire.

03:55.443 --> 03:57.654
- Oh, no!
- Run!

04:02.283 --> 04:03.201
Hurry up!

04:06.871 --> 04:08.248
ONE PER PERSON

04:09.540 --> 04:10.458
Let's go!

04:12.377 --> 04:14.504
Let's split up
and comb through the entire group!

04:14.587 --> 04:15.922
Don't let anyone escape!

04:16.005 --> 04:19.133
Are you really going to do this?
We were all allies!

04:19.217 --> 04:20.051
What?

04:20.134 --> 04:22.136
If the game doesn't end
after you hunt down everyone,

04:22.220 --> 04:24.013
then we'll eventually
have to kill each other--

04:26.182 --> 04:28.893
Burn him.
I have no need for useless people.

04:29.852 --> 04:31.145
Let's go!

05:49.724 --> 05:50.808
Suzuka, hurry up!

06:05.698 --> 06:08.868
We have no time to waste
with these people.

06:23.049 --> 06:24.884
Quick, hide inside this room.

06:24.967 --> 06:26.636
Where are you going, Usagi?

06:26.719 --> 06:28.721
I have to search for someone.

06:29.389 --> 06:30.640
Please bring me along!

06:30.723 --> 06:33.101
It's either Game Over or death for me
if I wait here.

06:35.228 --> 06:36.646
Hey, it's me!

06:39.524 --> 06:41.484
Let me help you!

06:41.567 --> 06:43.861
You and Arisu helped me in a game before.

06:48.241 --> 06:49.784
Help me search for Arisu!

06:53.996 --> 06:55.540
Those guys are serious about that.

06:55.623 --> 06:56.791
They're closing in.

06:56.874 --> 06:58.084
Let's hurry!

07:04.924 --> 07:05.967
Suzuka!

07:08.970 --> 07:11.264
Stop it. Neither of us is the witch.

07:15.977 --> 07:17.603
Hurry up and shoot.

07:20.231 --> 07:21.274
Please.

07:22.442 --> 07:23.818
Don't kill me.

07:24.986 --> 07:26.404
I'll do anything!

07:27.530 --> 07:30.491
Please. I beg you!

07:30.992 --> 07:33.369
That is not human.

07:34.454 --> 07:35.746
It's not a human!

08:42.438 --> 08:44.524
All of them are nuts.

08:47.276 --> 08:48.486
How unpleasant.

08:49.737 --> 08:51.614
Why would they go so far just to survive?

08:52.698 --> 08:55.993
There's no way
they'll find the witch like this!

08:59.997 --> 09:02.833
The witch could be you, Kuina.

09:05.920 --> 09:07.171
The same goes for you.

09:43.666 --> 09:45.543
Lure them all out to the courtyard.

09:46.127 --> 09:48.713
It's too troublesome
to move all the bodies.

09:49.797 --> 09:52.174
There are still some
hiding inside the hotel, right?

09:54.510 --> 09:56.053
I'll force them all out.

10:18.284 --> 10:20.119
- Arisu!
- Arisu.

10:21.912 --> 10:22.872
Arisu!

10:23.539 --> 10:24.498
Arisu!

10:26.125 --> 10:27.043
Arisu!

10:28.210 --> 10:29.211
Arisu!

10:30.504 --> 10:31.339
Arisu!

10:32.048 --> 10:38.971
GASOLINE, KEROSENE

10:56.113 --> 10:57.031
No!

10:59.033 --> 10:59.909
Asahi?

11:11.879 --> 11:12.838
Are you all right?

11:15.466 --> 11:16.926
I can't do this.

11:25.810 --> 11:27.311
Where is Arisu?

11:30.731 --> 11:32.358
He's in the main building.

11:36.987 --> 11:38.614
- Arisu!
- Arisu!

11:42.952 --> 11:44.453
Here we are!

11:58.050 --> 11:58.968
Joe.

12:01.303 --> 12:04.140
Fuck you, Saiko!

12:09.687 --> 12:11.313
Where is Arisu?

12:13.441 --> 12:14.650
Somewhere on…

12:16.444 --> 12:17.319
the fourth floor.

12:18.404 --> 12:20.072
You better be telling the truth.

12:20.156 --> 12:22.450
I saw Niragi coming out of a room.

12:50.352 --> 12:51.979
- Kuina?
- Hey.

12:52.813 --> 12:53.981
What are you doing?

12:54.523 --> 12:56.484
If you're free, can you lend me a hand?

12:57.109 --> 12:59.570
Are you the witch?

13:00.446 --> 13:01.363
Unfortunately, no.

13:03.324 --> 13:04.366
What about you?

13:06.994 --> 13:08.037
I guess not.

13:10.164 --> 13:12.333
Anyone who's desperately trying
to identify the witch now

13:12.416 --> 13:13.584
is not the witch.

13:14.168 --> 13:15.044
If you were the witch,

13:15.127 --> 13:16.962
you would have hidden yourself
to kill some time

13:17.046 --> 13:18.839
or participated in the killings.

13:19.757 --> 13:21.759
So what are you up to?

13:22.927 --> 13:24.220
Searching for the witch.

13:27.014 --> 13:28.057
Here it is.

13:28.682 --> 13:29.600
What's that?

13:30.226 --> 13:32.353
Cyanoacrylate glue.

13:32.937 --> 13:34.313
In short, super glue.

13:34.897 --> 13:35.856
What?

13:36.899 --> 13:40.236
If we heat this up
and hold it over the murder weapon,

13:40.319 --> 13:45.241
the cyanoacrylate vapors will fuse
with the moisture to show fingerprints.

13:45.825 --> 13:46.784
Fingerprints?

13:48.202 --> 13:51.205
Next, we'll use some cocoa powder
to dust for fingerprints

13:51.288 --> 13:54.083
on things like cups that have been used
by the most likely suspects.

13:54.166 --> 13:56.252
After we take the fingerprints with tape,

13:56.335 --> 13:57.962
we'll be able to identify the culprit.

14:00.089 --> 14:01.924
Just what did you do before coming here?

14:02.007 --> 14:04.343
I was in Forensics
in the Tokyo Metropolitan Police.

14:05.553 --> 14:08.639
I see. So we can clear the game like this.

14:19.191 --> 14:20.901
You, go ahead.

14:21.861 --> 14:22.736
What?

14:24.029 --> 14:26.866
I'll leave it to you
to help us clear the game.

14:33.080 --> 14:34.373
Fire!

14:41.714 --> 14:42.840
Over here!

14:46.135 --> 14:47.803
Someone, help us!

15:19.168 --> 15:21.545
- Run!
- Hurry up!

15:21.629 --> 15:22.880
Run to the annex!

15:29.386 --> 15:30.471
Damn it!

15:57.081 --> 15:59.083
Hey, aim properly!

16:01.043 --> 16:04.463
Take your aim!

16:04.546 --> 16:06.006
Take this!

16:06.090 --> 16:08.884
- Did you see that?
- Hey!

16:08.968 --> 16:12.304
I told you not to move!

16:12.388 --> 16:13.222
Hey!

16:14.390 --> 16:16.809
If you move again,
we'll make you eat that again.

16:17.559 --> 16:19.436
Urine rice!

16:21.855 --> 16:23.857
- Who's going next?
- I'll go!

16:23.941 --> 16:27.403
Hey, stand up! Come on!

16:27.486 --> 16:29.571
Are you listening, Niragi?

16:35.285 --> 16:39.206
Aren't you sick
of bullying the weak already?

16:41.834 --> 16:43.669
Where were you hiding?

16:44.753 --> 16:46.922
There are tons of places for me to hide.

16:48.465 --> 16:50.801
You really get on my nerves.

16:50.884 --> 16:52.636
All the goddamn time!

16:53.637 --> 16:55.556
You always act as if you're so clever.

16:57.307 --> 16:58.767
But I am clever.

17:03.731 --> 17:05.357
Perfect.

17:10.029 --> 17:11.822
Let's put an end to this, shall we?

19:09.398 --> 19:10.232
Not bad.

19:11.525 --> 19:13.110
What did you do before coming here?

19:14.486 --> 19:16.280
I worked in a clothes shop. Why?

20:06.747 --> 20:08.707
Never hesitate to land the final blow.

20:50.540 --> 20:52.251
- Damn junk!
- Stop it!

20:55.045 --> 20:58.090
You're a boy,
so why do you need cosmetics?

21:08.725 --> 21:09.685
Hikari.

21:11.144 --> 21:12.479
Never come back.

21:31.123 --> 21:33.375
Hikari? Hey!

21:53.937 --> 21:55.314
Enough about me.

21:58.775 --> 22:00.068
What about you?

22:05.699 --> 22:08.535
The main power supply has changed
since the game started.

22:08.618 --> 22:09.578
So?

22:10.162 --> 22:12.039
Our electricity used to be
powered by generators.

22:12.122 --> 22:14.708
Now it comes from the hotel's
main power source.

22:16.084 --> 22:20.797
This means that the ones in charge
of the game snuck into the Beach

22:21.673 --> 22:23.425
to control the power in the basement.

22:24.801 --> 22:26.053
What are you trying to say?

22:26.553 --> 22:28.972
I'm talking about
who the witch is, of course.

22:29.681 --> 22:30.974
What else do we need to care for?

22:31.808 --> 22:33.560
You're insinuating
that I'm the witch, right?

22:33.643 --> 22:35.145
Sorry, but that's not possible.

22:36.271 --> 22:40.942
Only the executives have information
on the main power supply management.

22:41.026 --> 22:45.947
In the first place, only you guys
have the key to access the underground.

22:47.532 --> 22:50.702
So I'll kill all executive members,
starting with you.

22:52.746 --> 22:55.582
Do you think that I can't aim
at a short range with this rifle?

22:55.665 --> 22:56.708
Yep.

22:58.919 --> 23:00.003
You idiot!

23:04.716 --> 23:05.884
What the hell was that?

23:28.615 --> 23:30.784
Robert Edwin Peary.

23:30.867 --> 23:34.913
He was an explorer who devoted
his entire life to reach the North Pole.

23:34.996 --> 23:36.498
THE BOUND UNIVERSE

23:36.581 --> 23:41.211
He failed many times, and even lost
eight of his toes to frostbite.

23:42.045 --> 23:43.505
However, in 1909,

23:43.588 --> 23:47.134
he became the first Westerner
to reach the North Pole.

23:50.929 --> 23:53.390
I'm leaving your dinner here.

24:00.272 --> 24:03.233
Ordinary people wouldn't understand

24:03.316 --> 24:05.569
those like him, who embrace death.

24:06.987 --> 24:10.740
However, I can tell
that they were shouting

24:10.824 --> 24:13.660
about their freedom of living,
which includes such death.

24:14.995 --> 24:16.329
What about me now?

24:16.413 --> 24:17.289
Hey.

24:19.583 --> 24:22.627
What should Mom do?

24:31.678 --> 24:37.309
Born in a land where I can't even
eat raw liver through my own volition,

24:37.934 --> 24:40.562
I was raised in an environment
that makes me unaware of death.

24:41.646 --> 24:43.565
How can I feel truly alive?

24:48.278 --> 24:50.030
Let me out of this temporary home.

24:51.823 --> 24:54.993
I want to live in the real world.

25:08.381 --> 25:12.010
And then, I came to this land.

25:30.862 --> 25:34.241
Game cleared. Congratulations!

25:43.959 --> 25:46.044
This is the first time
I have ever tasted it.

25:47.087 --> 25:48.255
The freedom of living.

26:41.099 --> 26:41.933
You.

26:43.018 --> 26:45.729
I heard that you were a tattoo artist
in the original world.

26:48.356 --> 26:49.190
Yes.

26:52.110 --> 26:54.321
Tattoo something really awesome
all over my body.

26:56.948 --> 27:00.869
Something so awesome that I won't be
able to live in the original world.

27:09.669 --> 27:11.296
This is my declaration of will.

27:12.839 --> 27:16.301
I will live in this land forever.

27:25.727 --> 27:26.728
For me…

27:29.105 --> 27:30.106
I have no past.

27:43.078 --> 27:44.245
Oh, sorry.

27:45.372 --> 27:46.873
I finally understand.

27:48.708 --> 27:51.544
I've always thought
that you and I were similar.

27:52.712 --> 27:53.880
Me and you?

27:57.884 --> 28:00.011
Both of us despise our past.

28:04.516 --> 28:06.976
I've finally decided because of you.

28:08.436 --> 28:11.147
You just keep turning your back
on your past.

28:12.273 --> 28:13.441
But I…

28:14.234 --> 28:16.653
I will face my past once more
in order to survive!

29:54.709 --> 29:57.545
Do you remember that arcade
that went down?

29:57.629 --> 29:58.797
What was the name again?

29:58.880 --> 30:00.673
It was in front of our high school, right?

30:01.382 --> 30:03.343
- What was it again?
- Dream World?

30:04.093 --> 30:05.386
It was Dream World!

30:06.012 --> 30:08.348
Oh, right! It was Dream World!

30:10.767 --> 30:13.853
I'd always skip classes to go there,
and Arisu would be there too.

30:13.937 --> 30:16.439
He would be
reading out loud all the dirty articles.

30:17.190 --> 30:19.400
The porn magazines from the '90s
were really the best.

30:19.484 --> 30:21.903
Right, they had big dreams.

30:22.487 --> 30:24.489
The reader submissions
were taken seriously.

30:24.572 --> 30:26.032
They really sucked you in.

30:27.534 --> 30:29.035
When the arcade went bankrupt,

30:29.118 --> 30:32.038
Arisu stood
in front of the building and cried.

30:32.121 --> 30:33.540
I didn't cry!

30:36.334 --> 30:39.712
Those times were the best.

30:39.796 --> 30:42.799
No matter how we complained,
high school life was awesome.

30:46.302 --> 30:47.262
Arisu.

30:49.889 --> 30:51.516
Live your life to the fullest.

30:54.769 --> 30:57.230
Live your life for me, got it?

32:24.275 --> 32:25.360
Someone…

32:27.278 --> 32:28.112
Someone…

32:31.491 --> 32:32.450
Smoke?

32:34.327 --> 32:35.787
What? Is there a fire?

32:38.331 --> 32:39.332
I hear someone.

32:47.215 --> 32:48.341
Hey!

32:49.509 --> 32:50.843
Someone, help me!

33:08.486 --> 33:09.821
Someone, help me!

33:11.072 --> 33:11.948
He's in there!

33:12.657 --> 33:13.658
Arisu!

33:14.701 --> 33:15.827
The door won't budge.

33:43.563 --> 33:44.731
I did it.

33:44.814 --> 33:46.107
I can't do this anymore.

34:00.997 --> 34:01.831
Arisu!

34:03.791 --> 34:04.709
Usagi.

34:43.206 --> 34:45.708
Is that all you can do?

34:47.710 --> 34:50.088
I knew it. You and I…

34:51.672 --> 34:53.174
Our will to survive is too different.

34:56.385 --> 34:57.470
"Will to survive."

34:58.888 --> 34:59.889
Was it?

35:24.372 --> 35:25.414
Hikari.

35:40.930 --> 35:43.516
You came back a totally different person.

35:51.149 --> 35:52.108
But…

35:54.402 --> 35:57.321
you look beautiful.

36:22.763 --> 36:23.598
Mother.

37:29.705 --> 37:31.832
"Never hesitate to deal the final blow."

37:32.917 --> 37:34.210
I did as you told me,

37:35.294 --> 37:36.254
Father.

37:49.392 --> 37:50.559
I'm so glad.

37:51.352 --> 37:52.311
You're safe.

37:52.895 --> 37:53.813
Thanks.

37:55.815 --> 37:59.068
I hate to break this to you now,
but we only have 30 minutes left.

38:01.070 --> 38:02.780
Just explain the rule to me.

38:11.872 --> 38:12.999
Out of ammo.

38:15.251 --> 38:18.838
We killed so many
and still can't find the witch.

38:23.843 --> 38:25.553
Just what have we done?

38:27.888 --> 38:30.057
This is seriously the worst rule ever.

38:31.642 --> 38:34.061
But just like those taggers
from the tag game,

38:34.603 --> 38:38.607
who were made to participate
in the game with rules of their own.

38:39.191 --> 38:42.236
I'm sure it's the same this time.

38:42.945 --> 38:45.406
The witch has to kill the girl
to start the game

38:45.990 --> 38:48.075
and survive
until the end of the time limit.

38:48.159 --> 38:51.370
In other words, the witch clears the game
if everyone here gets a Game Over

38:51.454 --> 38:52.955
or gets struck by the lasers.

38:53.539 --> 38:55.082
Just who could be the witch?

38:55.916 --> 38:57.626
If I were the witch,

38:58.627 --> 39:02.715
I would join the others in the hunting
since it'll be Game Over if I'm caught.

39:03.841 --> 39:06.302
So could it be someone from the militants?

39:07.178 --> 39:09.472
Niragi, Last Boss, or Aguni?

39:09.555 --> 39:13.726
No. If that's the case,
then the militants will kill one another.

39:13.809 --> 39:16.812
But it doesn't feel like
the purpose of the game.

39:17.396 --> 39:18.939
The purpose of the game?

39:19.023 --> 39:20.441
This is a Ten of Hearts.

39:21.942 --> 39:23.569
It's not just a physical game.

39:24.528 --> 39:26.864
I know that
since I've cleared a Hearts game before.

39:27.406 --> 39:29.283
Hearts games are utterly wicked.

39:29.867 --> 39:31.452
You toy with people's feelings,

39:32.495 --> 39:35.247
betray, and kill each other.

39:36.540 --> 39:39.710
They're designed so that you can't win
without feeling disgusted.

39:41.420 --> 39:45.466
If the militants win this way,
there will not be any conflict.

39:46.509 --> 39:48.135
So what is it?

39:51.889 --> 39:53.349
Something's weird.

39:55.434 --> 39:56.435
What could it be?

40:00.606 --> 40:01.899
If I were the witch,

40:03.067 --> 40:06.028
how would I influence the game?

40:55.244 --> 40:56.871
It doesn't suit you.

41:01.083 --> 41:03.419
Who would've thought
that the best host in Kabukicho

41:03.502 --> 41:04.795
would end up being a hatter?

41:06.130 --> 41:08.257
I can't go against my father's dying wish.

41:10.176 --> 41:12.428
You're an SDF officer too, right?

41:14.305 --> 41:16.807
I thought
you could only belong to the yakuza.

41:19.477 --> 41:20.644
Speaking of the yakuza,

41:21.437 --> 41:24.899
Shogo was killed laying his hands
on the government's money.

41:31.614 --> 41:34.992
You're the only old friend I have left.

41:36.410 --> 41:37.536
Live long.

41:40.289 --> 41:41.415
You too.

42:04.271 --> 42:05.272
No.

42:07.274 --> 42:11.028
I shouldn't be thinking like the witch.

42:11.737 --> 42:14.156
I should be thinking like the game master!

42:15.282 --> 42:16.325
Game master?

42:16.951 --> 42:19.703
Don't you think this seems tailor-made

42:19.787 --> 42:21.830
for the players, for this place,
and for this time?

42:22.790 --> 42:24.542
After Hatter was killed,

42:24.625 --> 42:25.876
Momoka was murdered.

42:26.585 --> 42:28.712
Someone who knows
the ins and outs at the Beach

42:28.796 --> 42:30.589
made this game
after calculating the timing.

42:31.632 --> 42:33.551
They calculated the timing?

42:33.634 --> 42:36.554
Their deaths did not just occur
at the same time by chance.

42:38.889 --> 42:42.393
The game master had likely been
waiting for this moment.

42:43.227 --> 42:44.478
Seriously?

42:45.938 --> 42:47.523
Then who is the witch?

42:49.441 --> 42:53.529
Hatter's death was made known
after Momoka died.

42:54.780 --> 42:56.949
Those who knew of Hatter's death

42:57.825 --> 43:00.452
were only the militants
and the executive members.

43:00.536 --> 43:06.375
But the game master might have
known of Hatter's death somehow.

43:07.376 --> 43:10.838
Then all the Beach members are suspects.

43:11.755 --> 43:15.009
When I passed by the lobby
one hour before the game started,

43:15.968 --> 43:17.761
Momoka's body wasn't there yet.

43:19.847 --> 43:23.350
So someone moved her body
during that time frame.

43:23.976 --> 43:26.854
There's no point in asking
since the witch can lie.

43:26.937 --> 43:28.063
The question is…

43:30.691 --> 43:33.152
Why did the game start now?

43:34.987 --> 43:36.780
Why did they wait for Hatter's death

43:37.573 --> 43:39.033
before they started the game?

43:40.826 --> 43:44.705
It was to throw the Beach
into a state of chaos.

43:45.414 --> 43:50.252
If that was the case,
if I were the game master…

44:16.028 --> 44:17.029
Don't tell me…

44:19.198 --> 44:20.240
I got it!

44:27.998 --> 44:30.668
If we stop here,
then all we did would be pointless.

44:30.751 --> 44:31.877
We can't stop now!

44:42.054 --> 44:44.473
Time remaining, 20 minutes.

44:58.570 --> 44:59.697
Arisu.

45:04.034 --> 45:05.285
I think I know…

45:07.579 --> 45:08.872
who the witch is.

47:13.497 --> 47:16.542
Subtitle translation by: Qianni Lu
